# holt Team — commercial license

The files in `src/team/` are **not** covered by the repository's FSL-1.1-MIT license. They are
source-available under the following terms:

- You may read, audit, and modify these files for internal evaluation and security review.
- Running them in the course of your work requires a valid holt Team or Enterprise license
  (see [current plan details](https://raed2180416.github.io/holt/#pricing)).
- You may not redistribute them, and you may not remove or circumvent the entitlement check.

Everything outside `src/team/` — the entire holt CLI, MCP server, TUI, scanner, safety
mechanisms and analysis engine — is licensed under
[FSL-1.1-MIT](../../LICENSE.md) for its defined Permitted Purposes, including internal commercial
use that is not a Competing Use. Each covered release converts to MIT on its own second
anniversary.

Questions: open a licensing request in the project owner's
[GitHub issue tracker](https://github.com/Raed2180416/holt/issues/new?labels=team-plan&title=Licensing+question).
